title the family that never printed -- a census with no denominator, and 222 systems carrying no clock
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think Reds-first found no row this lane can close. Of the five open rows, %291 and %295 are gated on Keaton's word, %301 is five booked folds whose remaining rooms sit inside the peer's live edit surface, %306 is Pond's, and %311's two ratchets are lowering-side repairs under Sound's language custody. Reporting that plainly is the honest act, and the lap went looking for its own work instead.
think The charter's Lindy-first item 1 -- the roster hears the language -- read as already landed: the six unreached Glow witnesses were seated 20260827.183635 on Keaton's word, and comlink_rehearsal_wire joined 20260828.011621. So I asked the smaller question the fire row asks, which is what my own lane's guards are reached by. Of 36 comlink, mantra and tablecloth witnesses, exactly one carries a roster row and 28 are reached by nothing at all.
think Pressing on that boundary is what found the real defect, and it was not in my lane. tools/fixtures/witness_reach_scan.sh gates one number over the whole tree, and its --families diagnostic piped through head -20 and printed absolute counts with no denominator. So `86 hunk` read as a big family with a tail, when every one of hunk's 86 witnesses is unreached; and the 224 other families holding an unreached witness never printed at all. comlink at 4 of 5 and mantra at 6 of 7 were invisible in the census a reader would open to look for them.
think The mechanism, plainly. families() in the scan now joins the unreached set against the whole set per family and prints `share unreached/total name` for every family rather than twenty; two readings, families= and wholly_unreached=, join the WITNESS_REACH summary line, appended at the end so no existing parser moves; and FAMILY_CEILING, overridable by WITNESS_REACH_FAMILY_CEILING for the control alone, gates the second at 222 under a ceiling that only falls. Measured on this tree: 222 of 291 families have every member unreached.
think Why the second number earns its own gate rather than riding on unreached: delete a family's only REACHED member and total falls by one and standing falls by one, so unreached -- which is total minus standing minus cadence -- stands exactly still while the family loses its last clock. That case is structurally invisible to the total, and the control proves it by doing it in the pen rather than arguing it.
think The rota read row 2, Fire/Mars, cut and stop, sense of sight: the threshold plus standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3622 and 3622 mod 5 is 2; the previous Silence lap read row 1, so a clean advance and no hand-advance. The row governed the lap in one sentence -- look hard at the thing most laps would rather route around -- and a green ratchet reading 1,140 under 1,154 is exactly that thing. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom: %301 was a meter blind to rooms it never discovered, and this is the same blindness one layer up, in the witness meter's own diagnostic.
obs I checked the control bites rather than assuming it, and the first check I wrote was wrong in a way worth recording. `census: prints every family, none dropped` failed on a correct scan, because my count of expected families read the scan's own summary line as a family: --unreached prints declared_enumerators and the WITNESS_REACH line beside its rows, and awk '{print $2}' turned `total=3` into a family named total=3. The scan was right and my check was sloppy; it now reads only rows whose first field is `unreached`.
obs The control's pen held three families, so the head -20 truncation this whole lap exists to refuse could have been put straight back with every check still green. That is a control proven in the passing direction only, which this tree already calls indistinguishable from a bypass. Twenty-five single-witness families are planted now, and with them the truncation regression flips the check. Both regressions were then planted in a full copy -- the truncation, and dropping the no-reached-member condition -- and both were refused, 42 of 42 otherwise green.
obs Peer named at the open per %291 and told twice before any file moved: grain-38, holding construction/ITINERARY.md, construction/SHRED_PREP.md, the day-shelf index, and an untracked log of its own. That index is the one file my lap and its lap both need. Committing it from here would carry the peer's uncommitted row -- pointing at a log git has never seen -- into my commit, so I proposed an order instead and stayed off all three of its files. My commit is path-limited to four files the peer is not in.
obs No clean roster reading, said plainly. The cold standing_equipment_run.sh opened at lap start has been alive close to an hour with zero output while the peer commits continuously, so it is bound to refuse under run_verdict=tree_moved. That is %295 and %291 territory rather than a new red, and it is the second Silence lap in a row to record it. The scoped guards that watch what I changed ran instead and are green.
obs The ledger headline is a second act that only one guard watches, and it caught me. Booking %316 left `Rows: 315` standing, and reds_ledger_monotone_witness refused with headline_drift naming all three disagreeing numbers -- total, span, and the derived remainder. Republished to 316 and 296 with the count stamp moved, and the witness is GREEN.
obs Said plainly rather than claimed green: equinox_e123_living_pin_guard REFUSES, with verdict=misread and detail=pin_over_bound on construction/REDS.md. It was refusing before this lap -- REDS.md stood at 28,568 bytes at HEAD against the 24,576 it declares -- and my row deepened it to 30,872. I did not fold it. The jam is the seat already named on the card: the pin keeps what is open, reds_fold.sh refuses any row carrying the bare word OPEN, and five rows carry it, so a closed-by-accretion row never folds either. That is Keaton's word rather than a lap's to force, and a fold attempted beside a live peer in one checkout would be %281 by another road.
obs Found and not taken: my lane's own 28 unreached witnesses are the work this census now makes visible, and seating them is a cost decision rather than a free one. Every one builds through Zig, and running twenty-eight builds beside a live peer in one checkout is %281 by another road. That lap wants a quiet tree, and it wants Keaton's word on the tier.
