recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two doors, neither mine. The day-shelf index is held by grain-38 with an uncommitted row pointing at an untracked log, so my index row waits on that lap landing rather than being merged into my commit; and seating my lane's 28 unreached witnesses is a tier decision that wants both your word and a tree no second hand is building in. The four files are committed locally and green.
